 ## Overview
-Domain Repetition is a technique for creating infinite, periodic repetitions of an object in space by wrapping query coordinates using modulo arithmetic [S1, S2, unofficial]. It allows rendering an infinite grid of primitives by modifying the position before querying the base signed distance field (SDF) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Domain-transform methods](28-domain-transform-methods.md) by applying a coordinate transformation stage to tile geometry without increasing polygon count.
